From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CBOC-Vita <cboc-vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Failures that must not take the game down: scene entry, shader patching, GPU timer ring

 - gxm.c: init_depth_stencil_buffer returns false (and keeps nothing) when the depth or stencil surface cannot be allocated, where it
   used to memset a NULL pointer. scene_reset returns GLboolean: no memory for a framebuffer's depth or render target, or a refused
   sceGxmBeginScene, leaves no open scene (the state vglSwapBuffers leaves) and is not tried again for that framebuffer before the next frame.
   Draws, clears and blits skip themselves on the false (draw.c, misc.c, framebuffers.c). vglSetRobustScenes(0) restores the old behaviour.
 - draw.c: the draw is submitted only if the program for it exists (is_draw_legal is checked in every build; it was ignored with SKIP_ERROR_HANDLING).
 - custom_shaders.c / shared.h: a fragment program that could not be patched is not published with the key that says it is current (the draw was
   made with the previous blend function, or with no program at all); a vertex program that could not be patched is not drawn with the
   previous layout's program. Both patch functions return the sceGxm result and count failures (vglRobustFailures).
 - rt.c: a scene is never recorded over the GPU timer record the watcher still holds (vglRtSetRingGuard, default on); the frames that lost a
   record are published with timed = 0 (vglRtRingDrops).

